        <p class="pex">Claim. For an asteroid, diameter D (km), geometric albedo pV and absolute magnitude H are tied by D = 1329 km / sqrt(pV) × 10^(−H/5). In JPL's Small-Body Database (SBDB) as served on 2026-10-30, 138,086 asteroids have all three fields. For …</p>
